  title: The Persian Achaemenid Empire
  text: In the late 6th century BCE Darius the First of Persia conquered Gandhara and the Indus region, which became a province paying rich tribute. Persian contact brought the Aramaic script, from which Kharosthi developed, and influenced later Mauryan art and administration.
